		{
			"id": "HA8pDDDU",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 105.29372959897944,
			"y": 948.4696042845183,
			"width": 1694,
			"height": 350,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "aP",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1607580543,
			"version": 719,
			"versionNonce": 1749471729,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1772792502921,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "| #  | System / Use Case                               | CAP Choice | Why This Choice Is Important                                                       |\n| -- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1  | Banking system                                  | **CP**     | Financial data must always be correct; system may reject requests during partition |\n| 2  | Stock trading platform                          | **CP**     | Incorrect price or trade execution can cause huge financial loss                   |\n| 3  | Distributed databases (strong consistency mode) | **CP**     | Data integrity across nodes is critical                                            |\n| 4  | Airline reservation system                      | **CP**     | Prevents double seat booking                                                       |\n| 5  | Configuration management system                 | **CP**     | All services must read the same configuration                                      |\n| 6  | Social media feed                               | **AP**     | Slightly stale posts are acceptable if the platform remains available              |\n| 7  | DNS system                                      | **AP**     | DNS must always respond even if records are slightly outdated                      |\n| 8  | Online shopping cart                            | **AP**     | Cart must remain accessible even during replication delays                         |\n| 9  | Messaging systems                               | **AP**     | System should continue delivering messages even during temporary failures          |\n| 10 | News / content websites                         | **AP**     | Serving slightly outdated content is acceptable                                    |\n| 11 | Single-server SQL database                      | **CA**     | No distributed network; system can maintain both consistency and availability      |\n",
			"rawText": "| #  | System / Use Case                               | CAP Choice | Why This Choice Is Important                                                       |\n| -- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1  | Banking system                                  | **CP**     | Financial data must always be correct; system may reject requests during partition |\n| 2  | Stock trading platform                          | **CP**     | Incorrect price or trade execution can cause huge financial loss                   |\n| 3  | Distributed databases (strong consistency mode) | **CP**     | Data integrity across nodes is critical                                            |\n| 4  | Airline reservation system                      | **CP**     | Prevents double seat booking                                                       |\n| 5  | Configuration management system                 | **CP**     | All services must read the same configuration                                      |\n| 6  | Social media feed                               | **AP**     | Slightly stale posts are acceptable if the platform remains available              |\n| 7  | DNS system                                      | **AP**     | DNS must always respond even if records are slightly outdated                      |\n| 8  | Online shopping cart                            | **AP**     | Cart must remain accessible even during replication delays                         |\n| 9  | Messaging systems                               | **AP**     | System should continue delivering messages even during temporary failures          |\n| 10 | News / content websites                         | **AP**     | Serving slightly outdated content is acceptable                                    |\n| 11 | Single-server SQL database                      | **CA**     | No distributed network; system can maintain both consistency and availability      |\n",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "edwwpnve",
			"originalText": "| #  | System / Use Case                               | CAP Choice | Why This Choice Is Important                                                       |\n| -- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1  | Banking system                                  | **CP**     | Financial data must always be correct; system may reject requests during partition |\n| 2  | Stock trading platform                          | **CP**     | Incorrect price or trade execution can cause huge financial loss                   |\n| 3  | Distributed databases (strong consistency mode) | **CP**     | Data integrity across nodes is critical                                            |\n| 4  | Airline reservation system                      | **CP**     | Prevents double seat booking                                                       |\n| 5  | Configuration management system                 | **CP**     | All services must read the same configuration                                      |\n| 6  | Social media feed                               | **AP**     | Slightly stale posts are acceptable if the platform remains available              |\n| 7  | DNS system                                      | **AP**     | DNS must always respond even if records are slightly outdated                      |\n| 8  | Online shopping cart                            | **AP**     | Cart must remain accessible even during replication delays                         |\n| 9  | Messaging systems                               | **AP**     | System should continue delivering messages even during temporary failures          |\n| 10 | News / content websites                         | **AP**     | Serving slightly outdated content is acceptable                                    |\n| 11 | Single-server SQL database                      | **CA**     | No distributed network; system can maintain both consistency and availability      |\n",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
